  "name": "Question 13",
  "problem": "Which of the following functions is continuous on the interval $(-2,2]?$",
  "worked_solution": "The correct answer is the following.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13945275/assets/221f7b64094910a5c1037e7071826f27f2ea0472ea93a612e9d38f3c46f5ad27.png)\n\nIndeed, we have that $q(x)$ is continuous on the open interval $(-2,2).$ \n\nAdditionally, the function is left-continuous at $x=2.$ Hence, it is continuous on the interval $(-2,2].$\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x)$ is not left-continuous at $x=2.$\n\n- $g(x)$, $h(x)$, and $p(x)$ are not continuous at some point that lies inside the interval $(-2,2).$",
